  "notes": "Covenants as restated in the Fifth Amendment (Aug 9, 2022) conformed agreement; the Sixth (May 11, 2023) and Seventh (Oct 15, 2024) Amendments did not change Sections 6.16/6.17. The EBITDA measure is 'Consolidated EBITDDA' (adds back depletion). Its add-backs include taxes, interest, depletion, D&A, amortization of intangibles and organization costs, extraordinary non-cash expenses or losses, non-cash impairment expenses or losses, and Transaction fees and expenses. It does not add back stock compensation, restructuring, or projected cost savings and synergies. Acquired and disposed businesses are included or excluded on a pro forma basis. The Interest Coverage Ratio denominator includes Consolidated Lease Expense (rentals) as well as Consolidated Interest Expense. The Leverage Ratio is gross: Consolidated Indebtedness, with no cash netting. A covenant breach is an immediate Event of Default under 7.01(d), with no grace period and no cure. The $50,000,000 Liquidity tests (for investments and acquisitions funded with Borrowings) and the Liquidity of at least 20% of Commitments plus Leverage below 2.00x test (for Restricted Payments under 6.06(d)) are incurrence conditions, not maintenance covenants. The facility is secured and shares collateral pari passu with Note Purchase Agreement notes under an Intercreditor Agreement. The Seventh Amendment removed the Parent Notes springing maturity, removed the Parent Notes and Preferred Stock references, and fixed maturity at Oct 15, 2029. Section 9.16(iii) lets the Collateral Agent subordinate liens to liens permitted by Section 6.02 without lender vote. Pricing grid runs SOFR+3.50%\u20134.50% based on Leverage Ratio, with 0.25% floor.",
  "terms": [
