      "kind": "j_crew_blocker",
      "present": "no",
      "section": null,
      "quote": null,
      "summary": "The agreement has no unrestricted subsidiary concept and no specific restriction on transferring or exclusively licensing material IP. Asset transfers are governed only by the general asset-sale and investment covenants.",
      "quote_verified": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "serta_protection",
      "present": "partial",
      "section": "Section 9.02(b)",
      "quote": "change Sections 2.16 or 7.02 of this Agreement or Section 9.2 of the Security Agreement, if effective, in a manner that would alter the pro rata sharing of payments required thereby, without the written consent of each Lender",
      "summary": "Changing the pro rata sharing and payment waterfall provisions requires all lenders. There is no express each-affected-lender consent for subordinating the loans or liens. Section 9.16(iii) authorizes the Collateral Agent to subordinate liens to other liens permitted by Section 6.02.",
      "quote_verified": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "chewy_protection",
      "present": "partial",
      "section": "Section 9.16(ii)",
      "quote": "to release any Guarantor from its obligations under the Guaranty Agreement if such Person ceases to meet the definition of a Guarantor or ceases to be a Subsidiary as a result of a transaction permitted hereunder; provided that no release shall occur if such Guarantor continues to be a guarantor in respect of any other Material Indebtedness",
      "summary": "Guarantors may be released when they cease to meet the Guarantor definition, which is tied partly to wholly owned status, or cease to be Subsidiaries. However, no release occurs while the entity still guarantees other Material Indebtedness. There is no express rule that losing wholly owned status alone does not trigger release.",
      "quote_verified": true
    },
    {
